**Starting point:** an existing mobile app and the approved Enterprise Datadog access process.

**On this page:** obtain access, identify your app configuration, and understand which signals you will verify.

**Section outcome:** collect permitted app telemetry, investigate errors/performance, and connect eligible mobile requests to backend traces using the actual release identity.

> **Confidential — Enterprise internal use only.** Never send passwords, payment data, customer/order payloads, authentication headers, or unapproved personal data to telemetry. Use approved access and redact screenshots.

## 1. Know what each signal tells you

| Signal | Developer question |
| :--- | :--- |
| RUM — Real User Monitoring | Which view/action/resource experienced the problem? |
| Logs and handled errors | Which safe diagnostic event explains an application failure? |
| Crash reporting / Error Tracking | Where did the JS/native application fail, and is its stack readable? |
| Mobile vitals | Which release/view has responsiveness, startup, rendering, or stability problems? |
| APM — Application Performance Monitoring | Can this eligible mobile request be linked to an instrumented backend trace? |
| Session Replay, only if approved | Can a permitted, appropriately masked visual replay help investigate the journey? |

Enable and verify each required signal separately. RUM initialization alone does not enable every signal or guarantee every interaction is captured. [Datadog application monitoring](https://docs.datadoghq.com/real_user_monitoring/application_monitoring/).

