## 2. Add the SDK and application integration

The screen examples use explicit views/actions. The iOS wrapper also offers native crash reporting; enable it only when approved. SDKs may collect default metadata and diagnostics even without automatic interaction tracking. Review the enabled SDK features and captured fields; manual events still require consent and privacy review.

<Tabs>
<TabItem label="Android">

### A. Add the RUM dependency

In the **application module** `build.gradle.kts`, use an approved version in place of the marker:

```kotlin
val datadogVersion = "REPLACE_WITH_APPROVED_VERSION"

dependencies {
    implementation("com.datadoghq:dd-sdk-android-rum:$datadogVersion")
}
```

Use your version catalog if the project already has one. Sync Gradle; confirm the dependency resolves before adding code. [Android SDK setup](https://docs.datadoghq.com/real_user_monitoring/application_monitoring/android/setup/).

### B. Add a small initialization boundary

Suggested location:

```text
app/src/main/java/<your-package>/observability/
└── MobileObservability.kt
```

```kotlin
// Use your application's actual package declaration.
import android.content.Context
import com.datadog.android.Datadog
import com.datadog.android.DatadogSite
import com.datadog.android.core.configuration.Configuration
import com.datadog.android.privacy.TrackingConsent
import com.datadog.android.rum.Rum
import com.datadog.android.rum.RumConfiguration

object MobileObservability {
    // Call on the main thread from the existing Application startup.
    private var initialized = false

    fun start(
        context: Context,
        clientToken: String,
        applicationId: String,
        environment: String,
        service: String,
        variant: String,
        site: DatadogSite,
        sessionSampleRate: Float,
        consent: TrackingConsent,
    ) {
        if (initialized) return
        require(listOf(clientToken, applicationId, environment, service)
            .all { it.isNotBlank() }) { "Missing observability configuration" }
        require(sessionSampleRate.isFinite() && sessionSampleRate in 0f..100f)

        val configuration = Configuration.Builder(
            clientToken = clientToken,
            env = environment,
            variant = variant,
        ).useSite(site).setService(service).build()

        Datadog.initialize(context.applicationContext, configuration, consent)
        Rum.enable(
            RumConfiguration.Builder(applicationId)
                .setSessionSampleRate(sessionSampleRate)
                .build()
        )
        initialized = true
    }
}
```

**Build configuration:** ensure the merged Android manifest permits network access (`android.permission.INTERNET`). Check the actual release configuration, not only the debug manifest.

Call `MobileObservability.start(...)` **once from your existing `Application.onCreate()`**, after `super.onCreate()`, with values from your approved configuration. `variant` must match the variant associated with uploaded mappings; use an empty string when the application has no flavor variant. Do not add a second `Application` class. [Initialization and variant matching](https://docs.datadoghq.com/real_user_monitoring/application_monitoring/android/setup/).

When the application's consent state changes, pass its corresponding SDK value:

```kotlin
Datadog.setTrackingConsent(newConsent)
```

`newConsent` is the `TrackingConsent` value supplied by your consent flow. `PENDING` can collect and batch locally; use `NOT_GRANTED` when collection itself is not permitted. [Consent behavior](https://docs.datadoghq.com/real_user_monitoring/application_monitoring/android/setup/).

### C. Track the ordering screen and confirmed result

Add these calls to the existing screen lifecycle and successful-order handler:

```kotlin
import com.datadog.android.rum.GlobalRumMonitor
import com.datadog.android.rum.RumActionType

// Merge these members into the existing ordering Activity.
private val orderViewKey = Any()

override fun onResume() {
    super.onResume()
    GlobalRumMonitor.get().startView(orderViewKey, "Chicken Order", emptyMap())
}

override fun onPause() {
    GlobalRumMonitor.get().stopView(orderViewKey, emptyMap())
    super.onPause()
}

// Invoke from the existing handler after validating the confirmed receipt.
private fun recordConfirmedOrder(itemCount: Int) {
    if (itemCount <= 0) return
    GlobalRumMonitor.get().addAction(
        RumActionType.CUSTOM,
        "chicken_order.confirmed",
        mapOf("item_count" to itemCount, "outcome" to "confirmed"),
    )
}
```

This is an **Activity class-body fragment**; merge with existing overrides rather than declaring duplicate methods. For Fragments or Compose, bind to the actual destination lifecycle. Do not combine manual and automatic view tracking for the same screen. [Android custom views/actions](https://docs.datadoghq.com/real_user_monitoring/application_monitoring/android/advanced_configuration/).

