> **Confidential — Enterprise internal use only.** Use the approved account and integration. Only provide permitted repository context. Do not put credentials, customer/production data, signing material, or private logs into instructions or prompts. This setup does not change Enterprise privacy or access settings.

## 1. Enable Copilot in your IDE

Follow your platform tab. Reuse an existing approved installation; do not install a second assistant or extension from an unofficial publisher.

<Tabs>
<TabItem label="Android">

**IDE: Android Studio.**

1. Open **Settings → Plugins** and locate the official **GitHub Copilot** plugin through the approved installation process.
2. Install/update the approved compatible version and restart the IDE if prompted.
3. Open **Tools → GitHub Copilot → Login to GitHub** and complete authorization with the approved account.
4. Open the application repository and Copilot Chat. Confirm that Copilot access is available before configuring project instructions.

