If sign-in or entitlement fails, resolve it through the approved access/support process. Do not switch to a personal account to work around restrictions.

**Attach screenshot — Copilot available in the IDE, with account and repository identifiers hidden.**

## 2. Create the repository instruction file

Use this layout at the **application repository root**, not inside only `android/`, `ios/`, or a feature directory:

```text
<repository>/
├── .github/
│   └── copilot-instructions.md
├── docs/
│   └── engineering-rules.md
└── ...existing application files...
```

Repository-wide custom instructions use `.github/copilot-instructions.md`. An ordinary Markdown file in `docs/` is a reference, not automatically an instruction entry point. [Repository custom instructions](https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/copilot-in-your-ide/customize-copilot/configure-custom-instructions/add-repository-instructions-in-your-ide).

From the application repository, inspect existing files first:

```bash
# Run the complete block inside the intended application repository.
# The subshell stops on failure without closing your terminal.
(
  set -eu
  REPO_ROOT="$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"
  cd "$REPO_ROOT"
  git status --short

  if [ -f .github/copilot-instructions.md ]; then
    cat .github/copilot-instructions.md
  fi

  if [ ! -s docs/engineering-rules.md ]; then
    echo 'Missing or empty docs/engineering-rules.md; complete Engineering Rules first.' >&2
    exit 1
  fi
)
```

If the last command fails, return to [Engineering Rules](./engineering-rules.mdx) and assemble the shared block, platform additions, and project facts. If the instruction file already exists, merge the content below through review; do not overwrite it blindly.

In the IDE, create a `.github` folder directly under the repository root if absent, then create/edit `copilot-instructions.md` inside it. Paste only the Markdown contents from the next section, not the enclosing code fences. No YAML frontmatter is required for this repository-wide Markdown file. [Creating repository-wide instructions](https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/copilot-in-your-ide/customize-copilot/configure-custom-instructions/add-repository-instructions-in-your-ide).

## 3. Copy the repository instructions

Copy this complete block into `.github/copilot-instructions.md`, merging any existing compatible instructions:

```markdown
