**Attach screenshot — sanitized response references and the verification plan, with private identifiers hidden.**

## 6. Troubleshoot setup before generating code

| Problem | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| Copilot unavailable | Check approved account entitlement, plugin status, and connectivity through the supported access process. |
| Repository instructions absent | Check `.github/copilot-instructions.md` spelling/location, intended project root, saved content, and custom-instruction setting/support. |
| Shared rules not read | Provide the permitted file explicitly; a link is not guaranteed retrieval. |
| Wrong platform or conflicting guidance | Inspect personal, repository, and other applicable instructions. Resolve conflicts instead of adding contradictory prompts. |
| Invented commands or test framework | Supply the actual project facts and test setup; request a corrected plan before implementation. |
| Correct instructions referenced but poor code | Review the code and assertions. Instructions influence output; they do not replace compiler, tests, coverage, review, or CI. |

## 7. Review and maintain the configuration

Run the following commands from the application repository root. Inspect the diff before staging. Stage only the intended instruction files after confirming they contain no secrets or unapproved content:

```bash
git diff -- .github/copilot-instructions.md docs/engineering-rules.md

# Also inspect new/untracked files in the IDE; git diff does not show them.
git status --short

# Run only after reviewing both files.
git add -- .github/copilot-instructions.md docs/engineering-rules.md
git diff --cached -- .github/copilot-instructions.md docs/engineering-rules.md
```

Submit the reviewed change through [Branching & PRs](../architecture/branching-prs.mdx). Do not include unrelated staged files. After updating rules, open a fresh interaction and repeat the controlled verification for affected behavior.

