Compare the response with the provided rules and feature contract. Ask it to point to the relevant supplied sections where possible; inspect those sections yourself. A statement that the rules were read is not sufficient evidence of correct application.

**Expected result:** the plan preserves the selected platform and existing runner, uses the supplied behavior, acknowledges missing facts, and proposes no LLM generation in CI or external action. If it invents a contract or ignores an instruction, correct the context and repeat the controlled prompt.

**Attach screenshot — sanitized project references and verification response.**

## 6. Request one bounded change

Once verification is satisfactory, use a task prompt such as:

```text
Using the supplied rules and verified project context, draft the smallest
change needed for the agreed chicken-order test case.

Provide code grouped by its actual project file path and explain where each
fragment belongs. Reuse existing fixtures, selectors, contracts, and dependencies.
Identify missing information before generating code that depends on it.

Include the known local verification commands and expected assertions.
Label checks you did not execute. Return a draft for review; do not edit
project files, run commands, contact live services, or deploy.
```

Inspect the generated code before applying it. Run the actual project checks in the appropriate development environment; a ChatGPT explanation or generated report is not a test result. Submit the reviewed change through [Branching & PRs](../architecture/branching-prs.mdx).

This project setup is for engineering assistance. It does not grant local filesystem execution, automatically edit a repository, configure Bitrise, or authorize Sauce Labs/store actions. Those capabilities require their separately approved environments and workflows.

## 7. Diagnose missing context and keep it current

| Problem | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| Response ignores project rules | Confirm the chat belongs to the intended project and the instructions were saved. Reprovide the relevant permitted rule section and verify again. |
| A local path or private URL is treated as accessible | Ask for the specific content actually inspected. Provide the approved excerpt/file or authorized source; do not assume retrieval. |
| Old rules or interfaces appear | Identify the intended revision and remove/supersede stale project copies. Start a fresh task interaction with the current references. |
| Wrong platform or test runner | Supply the applicable platform additions and actual test configuration. Reject invented framework substitutions. |
| Project files/settings are unavailable | Ask the workspace owner to confirm access and supported features. Do not use a personal-account workaround. |
| Code is presented as tested without execution | Require the actual command/result evidence or a clear unverified label; run the checks in the proper development environment. |

When engineering rules change, review and refresh the ChatGPT project instructions and affected uploaded references. A repository commit does not automatically update an uploaded copy. Keep the same reviewed requirements in the [Copilot setup](./github-copilot-setup.mdx) when both tools are used.

